    "text": "To solve the expression \\(\\frac{1}{-6} \\cdot 6 \\cdot 7 + 8 \\cdot 2 \\div 8 \\cdot (7-1)\\), we will break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, let's simplify the expression inside the parentheses:\n\\[7 - 1 = 6.\\]\nSo the expression now becomes:\n\\[\\frac{1}{-6} \\cdot 6 \\cdot 7 + 8 \\cdot 2 \\div 8 \\cdot 6.\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the multiplication and division from left to right. Start with \\(\\frac{1}{-6} \\cdot 6 \\cdot 7\\):\n\\[\\frac{1}{-6} \\cdot 6 = \\frac{1 \\cdot 6}{-6} = \\frac{6}{-6} = -1.\\]\nSo the expression now is:\n\\[-1 \\cdot 7 + 8 \\cdot 2 \\div 8 \\cdot 6.\\]\nSimplify \\(-1 \\cdot 7\\):\n\\[-1 \\cdot 7 = -7.\\]\nSo the expression now is:\n\\[-7 + 8 \\cdot 2 \\div 8 \\cdot 6.\\]\nNext, simplify \\(8 \\cdot 2 \\div 8 \\cdot 6\\):\n\\[8 \\cdot 2 = 16,\\]\n\\[16 \\div 8 = 2,\\]\n\\[2 \\cdot 6 = 12.\\]\nSo the expression now is:\n\\[-7 + 12.\\]\nFinally, simplify \\(-7 + 12\\):\n\\[-7 + 12 = 5.\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\\boxed{5}.\\]",
